<chapter xml:id="ch-main-scale-shapes" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Scale Shapes</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>Basic Scale Shapes with fingering on Free Bass and Treble Keyboard.</p>
    <p> Basic fingering and scale shapes on the right hand (treble) keyboard can be transposed to all keys in the first second and third columns (of a 5 column keyboard). The player can therefore choose amongst any one of the three basic shapes. The key is given by the starting note of each shape</p>
    <p> The free bass keyboard is limited to 4 columns and therefore only the first two basic shapes can be transposed to all keys. The third basic shape is only available in the keys of C and G major (ie; the first 2 left hand columns) on the free bass keyboard.</p>
  </introduction>
  

